                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A game for sickos. The adventure mode is hard enough, mostly just from poor design. How can anyone enjoy playing this with a timer and finite lives? I died so many times from not being able to know how my character was oriented in the room. I get that they’re doing a specific genre callback, 80s isometric puzzle adventure, but they designed this game with so many platforming elements in mind, and the isometric view makes a lot of rooms just awful to attempt.\n\nThat one big problem made it harder for me to overlook other smaller problems. The numerous pointless hallways, the dead air, the uninteresting puzzles, the irritating baby noise that your character makes on every single death. I was frustrated more than I was having fun. My favorite parts were definitely the platforming challenges, but they are timed and one-try-only, so when time runs out you don’t get to play again and the door to the challenges locks behind you. I failed all of them and could probably have succeeded with a second try but NOPE! Can’t do that.\n\nThere are clearly people out there who enjoy this game, but I am not one of them.",
